{"abstract":"A growing number of game design and development programs in higher education are beginning to incorporate environmental considerations into their curricula. This aligns with the broader push for more responsible and environmentally conscious practices in game production, consumption, and education. This article introduces two ongoing European inter-university projects: the Erasmus+ Greening Games project and the Nordplus-funded Nordic Alliance for Sustainability in Gaming network. Using them as case studies, the article reflects on the lessons learned and the challenges encountered while implementing the projects’ pilot stages, as well as their implications for environmentally conscious game design education more broadly.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fizek, Sonia","Fiadotau, Mikhail","Wirman, Hanna Elina","Garda, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677340"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Estonia","Finland","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tallinn University","University of Cologne","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Education","Game design","Green computing","Sustainability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teaching environmentally conscious game design lessons and challenges","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3583058","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677340","ids":["itu-f554da08-524b-4fdf-b8db-e293e90a9918"],"keyword":["Game design","education","green computing","sustainability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7407460B423648FBBCDB07DC36F7E185"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://orange.hosting.lsoft.com/trk/click?ref=znwrbbrs9_6-3074d_0x33b000x083678","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3583058","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cologne","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"university of turku","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Turku","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonia","key":"fizekpau","last":"Fizek","name":"Fizek, Sonia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikhail","key":"fiadotaupau","last":"Fiadotau","name":"Fiadotau, Mikhail","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna Elina","key":"wirmanpau","last":"Wirman","locid":"9ba013db-4c4d-41dd-be12-dbe188f67f29","name":"Wirman, Hanna Elina","orcid":"0000-0002-9578-2708","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gardapau","last":"Garda","name":"Garda, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3583058","issn":["28325516"],"issue":"1","jour